 Everything else returns `UNKNOWN_TYPE`: no login/logout, `chat:read` (sending read receipts), `message:unsend` (taking back), `message:react` (reactions), `channels:refresh`, sticker lists, or Token management. **Old messages are not replayed** (bots start from “now” and do not respond to history again; use `history:fetch` for history). No `read`, `update:available`, `api:state`, or `scam:state` is provided. Image/video and other media bytes are also inaccessible (bots see only the message's `contentType`).
 
 **Rate limits and risks**
 - Each connection is limited by `limits.sendsPerSecond` (≤5), and all bots together may not exceed `api.sendsPerMinute`; exceeding either returns `RATE_LIMITED`.
 - `scam:check` has its own limit of 10 per minute across all bots (separate from the web pages' budget); exceeding it returns `RATE_LIMITED`.
+- `chat:admins:get` is limited to 10 per minute across all bots (`RATE_LIMITED`); support is advertised in `hello.capabilities` as `"chat:admins"`. Non-OpenChat returns `CHAT_ADMINS_UNSUPPORTED`; missing metadata, repeated pagination tokens, more than 1000 pages or LINE failure returns generic `CHAT_ADMINS_FAILED`, never a partial list. Logout/account changes discard stale results. LINE offers no atomic cross-page snapshot, so membership changes during a scan can race; real LINE account behavior has not been exercised.
+- `scam:check` first rejects missing, non-text, unsent, undecryptable, system and known own messages from the local cache, without querying LINE membership for them. For other OpenChat messages, it resolves complete membership if own identity is unknown; failure never calls paid analysis. After waiting, it rereads and validates the current message, still rejecting own phone and bot messages. Actual mentions still use `message:send.mentions` (up to 20, UTF-16 offsets) and `replyTo`.
+- Concurrent analyses in the same login session and OpenChat share only an in-flight own-identity lookup. The slot is released on success or failure without automatic retries; logout invalidates shared state and stale results. Each message still consumes its own analysis quota and is analyzed separately. This shares no administrator grants: explicit `chat:admins:get` requests always perform a fresh lookup.
+- Admins returned in `chat:admins` may be mentioned even if they have never spoken, but only by the **same bot connection**, in the same chat, after its latest-started lookup succeeds. Starting another lookup immediately revokes the old list and supersedes any lookup still in flight; a superseded success returns `CHAT_ADMINS_FAILED` and cannot restore grants while the newer lookup is pending or after it succeeds or fails. Logout/account changes clear all grants. Arbitrary IDs remain forbidden. Query again before notifying to avoid stale roles.
 - Bots speak through **your personal account**. Frequent or mechanical sending may trigger LINE's risk controls. Set conservative limits and use a secondary account first.
 
